Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Tables tab is now venue-aware: pick a store, and its QR codes carry ?loc= so
  scanning sets the venue (menu, free categories, hidden-event access) AND the
  booth. Booth styles per venue: numbered ('Booth 1' with a custom word), a
  named list you paste in ('Microsoft Booth'), or both ('Booth 1 · Microsoft').
  Plain numbered 'Table' codes keep the bare ?table=7 so tickets still read 'T7';
  single-site deploys are unchanged.

- Kitchen tickets show a named booth as-is ('Microsoft Booth') instead of the
  numeric 'T7' prefix; numeric tables keep 'T7'. The booth is also stamped into
  the order metadata for reliable reporting.

- New 'Free coffees — who we gave them to' report in the Locations tab: every
  guest who took a complimentary coffee at an event, with their name, mobile and
  the booth they came from (e.g. 'Bill · 0404040404 · Microsoft Booth'). A live
  lead list derived from Square comp orders joined to their customer record.

